WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.566 --> 00:00:04.265
- [Voiceover] This is the Hyacinth Macaw.

00:00:04.265 --> 00:00:06.043
It's big, it's bright,

00:00:06.043 --> 00:00:09.827
and it's vulnerable to lots of threats.

00:00:09.827 --> 00:00:12.322
The largest parrot by length in the world,

00:00:12.322 --> 00:00:14.536
it can grow up to 40 inches.

00:00:14.536 --> 00:00:18.131
Their feathers are a
beautiful striking blue.

00:00:18.131 --> 00:00:20.763
Unfortunately, their
good looks have made them

00:00:20.763 --> 00:00:24.038
highly desirable in the illegal pet trade,

00:00:24.038 --> 00:00:26.371
fetching upwards of $10,000.

00:00:27.401 --> 00:00:30.887
Hyacinths are native to
Central and South America,

00:00:30.887 --> 00:00:32.523
primarily in the scrublands

00:00:32.523 --> 00:00:35.264
at the outskirts of the rainforest.

00:00:35.264 --> 00:00:36.962
It is an affectionate bird,

00:00:36.962 --> 00:00:38.724
but its powerful beak carries

00:00:38.724 --> 00:00:41.860
over 200 pounds of
pressure per square inch,

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:44.594
strong enough to crack a coconut.

00:00:44.594 --> 00:00:47.476
Their diet in the wild
consists mostly of nuts

00:00:47.476 --> 00:00:49.506
from native palms.

00:00:49.506 --> 00:00:52.401
Beyond being a hot
commodity in the pet trade,

00:00:52.401 --> 00:00:54.507
Hyacinths are watching their habitat

00:00:54.507 --> 00:00:57.052
get converted to farmland,

00:00:57.052 --> 00:01:00.876
leaving them less and less space to live.

00:01:00.876 --> 00:01:03.513
This is the Hyacinth Macaw.

00:01:03.513 --> 00:01:06.263
(dramatic music)

